CRASH-07: size SortedNodes for every node

openqual() allocates SortedNodes with the segment-array size,
Nlinks + Ntanks + 1, but sortnodes() stores one entry per node at
positions 1 to Nnodes. A connected network has at least Njuncs links,
which hides the mismatch. A network with an isolated component can have
more nodes than links plus tanks, and the sort then writes past the end
of the array. Allocate Nnodes + 1 entries.

Apply from the root of an EPANET checkout at 83e25bb:
    git apply CRASH-07_fix.patch

diff --git a/src/quality.c b/src/quality.c
index 36c89b9..fb6e5a1 100644
--- a/src/quality.c
+++ b/src/quality.c
@@ -92,6 +92,7 @@ int openqual(Project *pr)
     qual->LastSeg = (Pseg *)calloc(n, sizeof(Pseg));
 
     // Allocate memory for topologically sorted nodes
+    n = net->Nnodes + 1;
     qual->SortedNodes = (int *)calloc(n, sizeof(int));
 
     ERRCODE(MEMCHECK(qual->FlowDir));
